# HTTPS proxy for testing the dev server from other devices on the LAN —
# iPhone motion/orientation APIs (used by the pass page's sky view) only work
# in a secure context, so plain http://<lan-ip>:4000 won't do.
#
# Usage: start the dev server (bin/dev), then in another terminal:
#
#     caddy run
#
# and open https://m5-macbook-pro.local:8443 on the phone (same Wi-Fi). The first
# visit warns about the locally-issued certificate — tap "Show Details" then
# "visit this website" to proceed. To make the warning go away entirely, trust
# Caddy's root CA on the phone: AirDrop
# ~/Library/Application Support/Caddy/pki/authorities/local/root.crt to it,
# install the profile, then enable it under Settings > General > About >
# Certificate Trust Settings.

https://m5-macbook-pro.local:8443 {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy localhost:4000
}
